# Task 154-001 Execution Plan — RubricRegistry Core Foundation

## Goal
Create `src/orchestra/rubric-registry.ts` as a new file with TaskType taxonomy, 3 rubric constants, 3 detection heuristics, and registry API. Foundation for Sprint 154 Bug B fix (coverage:null doc task false NO_GO).

## Files Modified
- src/orchestra/rubric-registry.ts (NEW)

## Approach

### 1. Imports
- `import type { Task, EvaluationRubric } from '../core/types.js'`
- No imports from result-evaluator.ts (no circular)

### 2. TaskType taxonomy
```ts
export type TaskType = 'audit' | 'document-write' | 'code-development';
```

### 3. Rubric constants (frozen)
- `CODE_RUBRIC` — clone of DEFAULT_RUBRIC (correctness 0.4 / test_coverage 0.25 / scope_compliance 0.2 / documentation 0.15)
- `AUDIT_RUBRIC` — audit_completeness 0.4 / finding_count 0.3 / citation_density 0.2 / migration_triage 0.1
- `DOC_WRITE_RUBRIC` — correctness 0.3 / word_count 0.25 / scope_compliance 0.25 / documentation_quality 0.2
- All `passingScore: 70`, `maxRetries: 0`
- Use `Object.freeze` to prevent runtime mutation (gaming prevention SECURITY note)

### 4. Detection helpers (scope-shape, i18n-neutral)
- `hasCodeDir(directories)` — internal predicate checking src/tests/lib presence
- `isAuditTask(task)`:
  - filesWrite length === 1
  - file starts with `docs/audits/` and ends with `.md`
  - directories MUST NOT include any path with `src/`, `tests/`, `lib/`
- `isDocumentWriteTask(task)`:
  - filesWrite length >= 1 AND every file starts with `docs/` ends with `.md`
  - NO file starts with `docs/audits/` (audit exclude)
  - directories MUST NOT include src/tests/lib paths
- `detectTaskType(task)`:
  - audit → audit
  - document-write → document-write
  - fallback → code-development

### 5. Registry API
- `RUBRIC_REGISTRY: Record<TaskType, EvaluationRubric>` — frozen map
- `getRubric(task)` → returns rubric per detected type
- `coverageOptional(task)` → true for non-code

### 6. SECURITY JSDoc
- Document that rubric weights are NOT config-overridable; gaming prevention

## Acceptance verification
- `tsc --noEmit` → must be clean
- No import from result-evaluator.ts (verify with grep)
- JSDoc on every exported entity
- Verify tests don't regress (`npx vitest run`)

## Risks
- TS strict mode: ensure ReadonlyArray immutability matches EvaluationRubric.criteria type (RubricCriterion[]) — may need cast on freeze
- Path matching: use forward slash, ensure trailing slash handling for directories

## Estimated impact
- ~200 LoC, single file, no API surface changes for other modules yet (Tasks 2-4 will wire it)
